{
  "id": "business-finance-and-break-even",
  "title": "Finance: Business Costs, Income and Break-even",
  "term": 1,
  "summary": "Fixed and variable costs, cost price and selling price, mark-up, income and expenditure statements, profit and loss, and break-even analysis with tables, formulas and graphs.",
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Costs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "**Fixed costs** stay the same no matter how many items are made (rent, salaries, insurance).",
        "**Variable costs** depend on the number of items made (ingredients, packaging, electricity used in production).",
        "**Total cost** = fixed costs + variable cost per item × number of items."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Selling price and mark-up"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "latex": "\\text{selling price} = \\text{cost price} \\times (1 + \\text{mark-up \\%}) \\qquad \\text{profit} = \\text{income} - \\text{total cost}"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Break-even"
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": "Break-even point",
      "text": "The number of items at which total income equals total cost: there is no profit and no loss. Selling more gives a profit; selling fewer gives a loss."
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "latex": "\\text{break-even quantity} = \\frac{\\text{fixed costs}}{\\text{selling price per item} - \\text{variable cost per item}}"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 1",
      "problem": "Lindiwe sells T-shirts printed with school logos. Her fixed costs are R3 000 per month. Each T-shirt costs R55 to make and sells for R120. (a) Write formulas for cost and income. (b) Find the break-even point. (c) What is her profit if she sells 80 T-shirts?",
      "steps": [
        "(a) Cost: $C = 3\\ 000 + 55n$; Income: $I = 120n$",
        "(b) $120n = 3\\ 000 + 55n \\Rightarrow 65n = 3\\ 000 \\Rightarrow n = 46{,}2$, so she must sell 47 T-shirts.",
        "(c) Income R9 600; cost R3 000 + R4 400 = R7 400; profit R2 200"
      ],
      "answer": "Break-even at 47 T-shirts; profit R2 200 for 80"
    },
    {
